  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14204584/assets/64ab493abc4e32afc36676b20cf0e8898c4d0ba07c086280e426890c7bdfb70a.png)\n\nNotice that the sequence is geometric, with a common ratio of \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{10}{2}=5.\n$$\n\nSo, we can get each term by multiplying the previous term by $5.$ \n\nContinuing to list terms of the sequence until we get to the $6$th term, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14204584/assets/32f60b73a942c4e792f3629b5f4824f1c639a25e03491a36f81679d126bcd685.png)\n\nTherefore, the $6$th term is $6250.$",
